, "Newest usable poll is 48 days old; polling uncertainty inflated."]}, "overview": "Utah's 1st District, redrawn after redistricting to include Salt Lake City, is the bluest corner of Utah, with a Democratic partisan lean of 12 points. Former congressman Ben McAdams faces Republican Riley Owen, a first-time candidate with minimal fundraising, in an open-seat race. McAdams has raised $2.8 million and benefits from $2.7 million in outside support, outspending Owen by more than $2 million in the final stretch.\n\nThe only public poll, from Lighthouse Research in early September, showed McAdams leading 63-21 among likely voters, and prediction markets price his win probability at 97-98 percent. Debates between the two moderates found considerable common ground, but the structural advantages favor McAdams decisively. The race is rated Safe Democratic, with modest uncertainty given the thin and aging polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9908, "margin": 20.9}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.99, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9893, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9909, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9906, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9886, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9907, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.99, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9979, "margin": 28.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.997, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9991, "margin": 28.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9988, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9979, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9971, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9972, "margin